# Workspace Plan Command

Use `workspace plan` to inspect the active plan reconstructed by the
`eventsourcing` repository.

Use `workspace plan start TITLE` to create the active plan. The command fails
when another active plan already exists.

Use `workspace plan agent` before authoring a stage. It reports the active stage
and the artifact paths that may be written.

Use `workspace plan put PATH` with stdin to write the current-stage artifact
through the plan module instead of editing files directly.

Use `workspace plan ask TITLE EXPLANATION` to record an open gate question for
the current stage.

Use `workspace plan answer TITLE ANSWER` to record a resolved gate question for
the current stage. Do not edit markdown artifacts to submit question state.

Use `workspace plan next` only after the current stage artifact and its resolved
question are present.

Use `workspace plan restore` to regenerate recorded projection files for the
active plan from the event stream.
